🟢 Topic 1: Terraform Basics (Foundation)
🔹 What is Terraform?

Terraform is an Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tool used to:

Create infrastructure
Update infrastructure
Destroy infrastructure
👉 using code instead of manual UI
🔹 What is IaC (Infrastructure as Code)?

Instead of creating resources manually in AWS:

❌ Clicking in console
✅ You write .tf files

👉 Benefits:

Version control (Git)
Reusability
Automation
Consistency
🔹 Terraform Core Concepts
1. Provider
Connects Terraform to platform
provider "aws" {
  region = "ap-south-1"
}
2. Resource
Actual infrastructure (EC2, S3, etc.)
resource "aws_instance" "myec2" {
  ami           = "ami-123456"
  instance_type = "t2.micro"
}
3. Variables
variable "instance_type" {
  default = "t2.micro"
}
4. Output
output "instance_ip" {
  value = aws_instance.myec2.public_ip
}
🔹 Terraform File Structure
main.tf        → main config
variables.tf   → inputs
outputs.tf     → outputs
provider.tf    → provider config
🔹 Install Terraform

👉 Download from:

Official site of HashiCorp

👉 Verify:

terraform -v
🔹 First Hands-on (Very Important 💯)
Step 1: Create main.tf
provider "aws" {
  region = "ap-south-1"
}

resource "aws_instance" "demo" {
  ami           = "ami-0f5ee92e2d63afc18"  # example
  instance_type = "t2.micro"
}
Step 2: Run Commands
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply

prompted

🔹 What Happens Internally?
init → downloads provider plugins
plan → shows execution plan
apply → creates infra

🔥 Mini Interview Insight
Terraform is declarative, not imperative
You define desired state, Terraform achieves it 